<title>INDIA: India's HOC, BPCL to set up phenol plant.</title>
<headline>India's HOC, BPCL to set up phenol plant.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Hindustan Organic Chemicals Ltd (HOC) and Bharat Petroleum Corporation Limited (BPCL) have signed an agreement to set up a new phenol plant with an annual capacity of 100,000 tonne, the Press Trust of India (PTI) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The proposed plant will be based on feedstocks sourced from BPCL. The joint venture is in the preliminary stages and the details in terms of technology tie-ups are still being worked out, PTI quoted an HOC spokesman as saying.</p>
</text>
